  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Qc9GqSOBw3aEHToRlGkueRwy1bI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:27:26.305Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "VASS carries three verticals on its row \u2014 banking, retail and public \u2014 and a tool field that reads \"not researched\". Its priority-4 position came from a mechanical rescore of a provisional v2 tail entry using size and slot occupancy, with no v3 evidence pass behind it.\n\nThe vertical mix is the only positive signal, and it is a generic one: banking, retail and public sector describe most large Iberian integrators. Without a platform record there is nothing that separates this row from its neighbours, and nothing that tells an outreach decision whether the firm has a slot to fill or a stack to defend.\n\nThe flag's instruction is therefore the whole finding: run the OSS-portfolio screen before acting. Doing that for VASS is cheap relative to a call, and it converts a rank that currently encodes company size into an actual position on the question the pilot cares about.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen**\n- VASS (ES)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> DERIVED, NOT SCORED ON v3 \u2014 v2 row rescored mechanically (size + slot-occupancy only). Run the OSS-portfolio screen before acting. v2 verticals: Banking, retail, public",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:27:26.304997Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:27:26.305007Z"
    }
  },
